Creative Catalyst: Its founding artists were botanists who sonified the electrical signals of rainforest plants.

Chlorovolt Rhapsody sounds like a grief-stricken 40-piece symphony and a blistering, virtuoso jazz-rock ensemble simultaneously tuning their instruments inside an electric storm in the deep Amazon. Complex, odd-meter fusion rhythms and overdriven Rhodes keyboards collide with weeping orchestral string crescendos, all warped, filtered, and steered by the erratic, microscopic electrical spasms of traumatized jungle flora.

